raw_response:
 Yes, I understand that you would like to know how to create a pop-up window on a website using HTML and CSS. Here are the steps to create a simple pop-up window:

1. Create a new HTML file and add a `<div>` element inside the `<body>` element. This `<div>` element will act as the pop-up window.
2. Add an event listener to the `<button>` element that will trigger the pop-up window. You can use the `addEventListener()` method to attach an event listener to the button.
3. Inside the event listener, add a function that will open the pop-up window. This function should use the `innerHTML` property to set the content of the pop-up window to a string that describes the pop-up.
4. Use CSS to style the pop-up window. You can use the `position` property to position the pop-up window relative to the button, and the `display` property to hide the pop-up by default.
5. Test the pop-up window by clicking the button.

Here is an example of the HTML and CSS code for a simple pop-up window:

HTML:
```php
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Pop-Up Window Example</title>
	<style>
		.popup {
			position: absolute;
			display: none;
			z-index: 1;
			top: 100px;
			left: 50px;
			width: 300px;
			background-color: #333;
			color: #fff;
			padding: 20px;
			text-align: center;
			border: 1px solid #888;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<button onclick="openPopup()">Open Pop-Up Window</button>
	<div class="popup">
		<p>This is a pop-up window.</p>
	</div>
	<script>
		function openPopup() {
			var popup = document.getElementById("popup");
			popup.style.display = "block";
		}
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```
CSS:
```css
.popup {
	position: absolute;
	display: none;
	z-index: 1;
	top: 100px;
	left: 50px;
	width: 300px;
	background-color: #333;
	color: #fff;
	padding: 20px;
	text-align: center;
	border: 1px solid #888;
}
```
This is just a basic example, and you can customize the pop-up window to suit your needs.

